Apply: git apply docs/pending-protected/blueprint-build.patch
1) extract: a repeatable build. The model is called at temperature 0 (+ fixed seed, no hidden reasoning on Kernal:
   llm.repeatable_kwargs), through blueprint.propose: when the saved map was built from exactly these inputs
   (its input_hash) it is returned without a model call; ?fresh=1 always asks the model (the 20-build proof uses it).
   One automatic retry on a timeout, 502, cut-off or unreadable reply; then 502/504 and the panel keeps the saved map.
2) extract: max_tokens 4000 -> 8000 and an explicit 'cut off' 502; papers are no longer read (they were not sent anyway).
3) 422 copy names the syllabus and the learning objectives, no past exams (the UI already overrides it client-side).
4) apply: BlueprintApplyIn keeps input_hash; a Save is checked against the course's own weeks/objectives and named
   after its own week titles (fixes the stored objectives_total/weeks_unmapped on a Save without scope).
5) card-tagging 422: 'exam blueprint' -> 'coverage map'.
Regenerated 2026-11-14 against main a261d32 (git apply --check passes). No schema change.

